<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{@site.locale}}" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="HandheldFriendly" content="True">
    <title>{{meta_title}}</title>

    {{!-- ── Pre-paint theme ───────────────────────────────────────────────
      The DESIGN SYSTEM's own bootstrap, generated into a partial by
      `yarn design:sync` so it cannot drift from the copy the Next.js app
      runs. It must stay the FIRST thing in <head>, before any stylesheet:
      it sets data-theme on <html> before first paint, and anything above it
      that blocks would paint the wrong colours first.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    {{> "ds/theme-init"}}

    {{!-- ── Fonts & icons: ALL self-hosted, ZERO third-party ──────────────
      Type used to come from Google Fonts and icons from unpkg's two full
      Phosphor fonts (~1,500 glyphs, 279 KB of woff2) — four render-blocking
      stylesheets across two origins.

      Now: one local stylesheet carrying the @font-face rules, and TWO
      preloaded fonts — the two the design system ships, both on the critical
      path because both are on screen in the first viewport.

        Switzer      the entire interface AND reading face — headings and body
                     separated by weight and size, never by two cuts.
        Roboto Mono  every index, duration, kicker, tag, status and <pre>.
                     Preloaded, not deferred: the mono voice is in the navbar,
                     the hero badges and the first curriculum row, so it is
                     first-viewport text on essentially every route.

      NO SHIPPED SERIF. The editorial register (pull-quotes, drop caps,
      section quotations) used to run on Sentient. The design system retired
      it — `--font-serif` now resolves to the platform's own serif — so the
      quoting voice still reads as a quotation everywhere Georgia exists and
      costs zero bytes. Do not re-add a serif webfont here; change
      NS-Design-System and re-sync if that decision is ever revisited.

      ICONS ARE INLINE SVG — {{> icons name="…"}}. No icon font, no icon
      request, no flash of blank boxes, and they inherit currentColor.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin href="{{asset "fonts/switzer-var-latin.woff2"}}">
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin href="{{asset "fonts/roboto-mono-var-latin.woff2"}}">

    {{!-- Theme stylesheet (Tailwind build) — carries the @font-face rules --}}
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "built/screen.css"}}">

    {{!-- ── Connection warm-up ────────────────────────────────────────────
      Only for origins this page will ACTUALLY hit, and only when they are
      switched on. A speculative preconnect to a domain the page never calls
      costs a DNS lookup, a TCP handshake and a TLS negotiation for nothing —
      and browsers cap how many they will honour, so a wasted one evicts a
      real one. Fonts and icons are same-origin, so they need none.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    {{#if @custom.enable_ads}}{{#if @custom.adsense_publisher_id}}
      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com" crossorigin>
    {{/if}}{{/if}}

    {{!-- Google AdSense loader — only when ads are enabled + a publisher ID is set
         (Ghost Admin → Design). Individual slots are placed via the ads/adsense partial. --}}
    {{#if @custom.enable_ads}}{{#if @custom.adsense_publisher_id}}
      <script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client={{@custom.adsense_publisher_id}}" crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
    {{/if}}{{/if}}

    {{!-- PWA: icons, manifest, theme colour (icon kit in assets/logo/) --}}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{asset "logo/favicon.svg"}}">
    <link rel="icon" href="{{asset "logo/favicon.ico"}}" sizes="48x48">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{asset "logo/apple-touch-icon.png"}}">
    <link rel="manifest" href="{{asset "logo/manifest.webmanifest"}}">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0176d3">

    {{!-- Ghost-injected SEO tags, structured data, code injection, search, etc. --}}
    {{ghost_head}}
  </head>

  <body class="{{body_class}} flex min-h-screen flex-col bg-surface text-ink">
    {{!-- Site header. Course/lesson/training posts get the distraction-free
         "course player" header (logo · progress · ✕ back-to-course); everything
         else gets the standard navigation bar. --}}
    {{#is "post"}}{{#post}}{{#has tag="#lesson, #training, #training-content, #training-section"}}{{> "components/course-player-header"}}{{else}}{{> header}}{{/has}}{{/post}}{{else}}{{> header}}{{/is}}

    {{!-- Custom @graph JSON-LD (navbar + site nodes). Placed after the header
         (before the footer's secondary-nav render) so {{#foreach navigation}}
         resolves to the PRIMARY menu. Valid for crawlers anywhere in the doc;
         additive to Ghost's own structured data. --}}
    {{> "jsonld/graph"}}

    {{!-- Page body — each template's content renders here --}}
    <main id="main" class="flex-1">
      {{{body}}}
    </main>

    {{!-- Site footer. Lesson/module posts get a minimal, distraction-free
         footer; every other page gets the full footer. --}}
    {{#is "post"}}{{#post}}{{#has tag="#lesson, #training-content, #training-section"}}{{> "footer-lesson"}}{{else}}{{> footer}}{{/has}}{{/post}}{{else}}{{> footer}}{{/is}}

    {{!-- PWA install prompt (shown by pwa.js when installable) --}}
    {{> "components/pwa-install"}}

    {{!-- Ghost-injected scripts: Portal (members), search, comments, etc. --}}
    {{ghost_foot}}

    {{!-- Expose current Ghost member data for PostHog user identification.
         UUID is a non-PII identifier; email/name are set as person properties
         (not event properties) inside posthog-init.js. --}}
    <script>
      window.__phMember = {{#if @member}}{
        id: '{{@member.uuid}}',
        email: '{{@member.email}}',
        name: '{{@member.name}}',
        subscribed: {{@member.paid}}
      }{{else}}null{{/if}};
    </script>

    {{!-- ── The design system's runtime ──────────────────────────────────
      Vendored by `yarn design:sync` into assets/js/ds/ — behaviour comes from
      the system for the same reason the CSS does. Each is an independent
      module on its own `defer` tag rather than concatenated into casper.js,
      so a page only pays for what it uses and load order stays explicit.

        nav    the top bar: menus, the mobile sheet, the theme switch, the
               scrolled state. Every page has a bar, so every page loads it.
        toc    the outline + scroll-spy — only where there is prose to outline.
        lms    the lesson rail, curriculum and reading progress.

      `defer` (not `async`) is deliberate: these run after parse, in order,
      and none of them block the first paint.
    ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    <script defer src="{{asset "js/ds/nav.js"}}"></script>
    {{#is "post, page"}}<script defer src="{{asset "js/ds/toc.js"}}"></script>{{/is}}
    {{!-- code.js wires [data-code="copy"] on the .ns-code figures that the
         theme's own assets/js/code.js builds out of Ghost's bare <pre>. --}}
    {{#is "post, page"}}<script defer src="{{asset "js/ds/code.js"}}"></script>{{/is}}
    {{#is "post"}}{{#post}}{{#has tag="#lesson, #course, #training-content"}}<script defer src="{{asset "js/ds/lms.js"}}"></script>{{/has}}{{/post}}{{/is}}
    {{!-- tabs.js implements the ARIA contract the CSS documents: roving
         tabindex, arrow keys, aria-selected + [hidden] on the panels. Without
         it the course page's tabs LOOK selectable and are not — and every
         panel stays visible, which is a longer page but never hidden content.
         That is why the panels are not hidden in the markup. --}}
    {{#is "post"}}{{#post}}{{#has tag="#course"}}<script defer src="{{asset "js/ds/tabs.js"}}"></script>{{/has}}{{/post}}{{/is}}

    {{!-- Alpine — still the tool for the catalog filters and the small
         disclosure state the system does not model.

         The `lessonNav` store is registered HERE, not in a partial, because
         four separate partials read it (courses/lesson-nav, training/
         curriculum, training/nav-button, training/section-item) and none of
         them is guaranteed to render first. It used to live in the course
         player's header, which meant the store existed only on the routes
         that happened to use that header. Registered on `alpine:init`, which
         still fires because this inline script is parsed before the deferred
         bundle runs. --}}
    <script>
      document.addEventListener('alpine:init', function () {
        window.Alpine && Alpine.store('lessonNav', {
          open: false,
          toggle() { this.open = !this.open; },
          close() { this.open = false; }
        });
      });
    </script>
    <script defer src="{{asset "js/vendor/alpine.js"}}"></script>

    {{!-- The theme's own remaining helpers (scroll reveal, pointer spotlight,
         count-ups) — concatenated and minified by gulp. --}}
    <script defer src="{{asset "built/casper.js"}}"></script>

  </body>
</html>
